  {
   "id": "sc8ycjfjPcEJ",
   "from": "Marco Inacio",
   "author": "484c91357ac83f6b",
   "date": "2014-12-14T01:39:06Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Hurdle Model from Manual",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>\r<br>&gt; How can y[n] be sampled from a Bernoulli if it is &gt;1?\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "You&#39;re right, if you follow the notation of manual for Hurdle \r<br>distribution, it should be:\r<br>\r<br>(y[n] == 0) ~ bernoulli(theta);\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "if (y[n] &gt; 0)\r<br>   y[n] ~ poisson(lambda) T[1,];\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Example:\r<br>\r<br>stanm2 &lt;- stan_model(model_code=&quot;\r<br>data {\r<br>   int y[3];\r<br>}\r<br>parameters {\r<br>   real&lt;lower=0, upper=1&gt; theta;\r<br>   real&lt;lower=0&gt; lambda;\r<br>}\r<br>model {\r<br>   for (n in 1:3) {\r<br>     (y[n] == 0) ~ bernoulli(theta);\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "     if (y[n] &gt; 0)\r<br>     y[n] ~ poisson(lambda) T[1,];\r<br>   }\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "}&quot;)\r<br>\r<br>fit1 &lt;- sampling(stanm2, chains = 2, iter = 1e4, data = list(y = c(1,2,0)))\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
